  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "The value of \\[ \\frac{1}{2-\\dfrac{1}{2-\\dfrac{1}{2-\\frac12}}} \\] is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\frac34\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\frac45\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\frac56\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\frac67\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\frac65\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Start with the innermost subtraction, since its value determines the next fraction. Working outward gives\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n2-\\frac12&=\\frac32,\\\\\n2-\\frac{1}{3/2}&=2-\\frac23=\\frac43,\\\\\n2-\\frac{1}{4/3}&=2-\\frac34=\\frac54.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nEach denominator is positive, so every reciprocal is defined. The requested value is therefore\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{5/4}=\\boxed{\\frac45},\n\\]\nchoice B.",
